Implement user story SKY-002-test: Write vitest tests for SkyscannerClient

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock the global fetch (no real network calls). Cover: URL/header construction, successful response parsing, HTTP error handling, missing API key errors, parse/validation errors, and explicit MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API mock mode behavior.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts uses vitest with mocked global fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) and afterEach restoration; no real network calls in any test
- Test verifies correct RapidAPI URL and header construction, including apiKey precedence over RAPIDAPI_KEY env var
- Test verifies successful API response is parsed into FlightResult[] matching the exported interface
- Test verifies HTTP 4xx/5xx responses cause searchFlights to reject with an Error containing the status code
- Test verifies missing or empty API key (constructor arg omitted, empty string, RAPIDAPI_KEY unset/empty) causes constructor to throw a descriptive Error referencing the missing key
- Test verifies malformed or missing-fields response body causes searchFlights to reject with a parse/validation Error
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns deterministic fixture without invoking fetch (spy/assert fetch never called); non-'true' values (unset, empty, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') perform real fetch — strict opt-in, not fuzzy truthy check
- vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- SkyscannerClient class exported from module
- Constructor signature: constructor({ apiKey }: { apiKey?: string } = {})
- Constructor throws Error with exact message 'Missing API key: provide apiKey or set RAPIDAPI_KEY' when resolvedKey is falsy or empty string
- API key resolution precedence: apiKey param > process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API env check uses strict equality 'true' — only exact string 'true' triggers mock, not 'TRUE', '1', or truthy values
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true', searchFlights returns deterministic mock data from #getMockFlights without calling fetch
- Mock flights array contains exactly 2 FlightResult objects with fixed values
- API endpoint URL: https://skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com/v3/flights/live/search
- Query params set: 'origin', 'destination', 'date', and optionally 'adults' if defined
- HTTP method: GET
- Request headers include 'X-RapidAPI-Key' and 'X-RapidAPI-Host'
- X-RapidAPI-Host header value: 'skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com'
- On non-ok response, throws Error with message 'Skyscanner API request failed with status ${response.status}'
- #parseFlightResults validates response structure and throws Error with prefix 'Failed to parse Skyscanner API response:' for various validation failures
- Validation errors include: 'response is not an object', 'results is not an array', 'result item is not an object', and field type checks for price, currency, airline, departure, arrival, duration, stops
- No validation on adults parameter range — accepts 0, negative numbers, or any number
- No validation on origin/destination format — accepts any string
- No validation on date format — accepts any string
- No retry logic on failed requests
- No timeout configuration on fetch calls

## Mock Strategy
```typescript
vi.mock('<import-path-to-SkyscannerClient>', () => ({
  SkyscannerClient: vi.fn().mockImplementation(() => ({
    searchFlights: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined),
  })),
}));
```

